Als Teamleider Luchtvracht X-ray werk je in de dynamische omgeving van Schiphol. Je stuurt een team van circa 20 beveiligers aan, bewaakt het proces en zorgt dat alles veilig en soepel verloopt. Je bent zichtbaar op de werkvloer en werkt actief mee.

Jouw werkzaamheden:

• Aansturen en coachen van een team van ±20 beveiligers;
• Bewaken van de voortgang en kwaliteit van de operatie;
• Oplossen van onverwachte situaties samen met het team;
• Functioneel leidinggeven aan X-ray screeners;
• Verantwoordelijk voor personele begeleiding en ontwikkeling;
• Actief meewerken in de dagelijkse operatie;
• Samenwerken met collega teamleiders voor optimale teamperformance.

• Je bent in het bezit van het diploma beveiliger 2 en/of coördinator 3 is een pré;
• Je hebt minimaal 2 jaar leidinggevende ervaring;
• Een zeer goede beheersing van de Nederlandse en Engelse taal;
• In het bezit van rijbewijs B of eigen vervoer;
• Je woont op maximaal 50 km van Schiphol;
• Je herkent je in onze kernwaarden: integriteit, waakzaamheid en behulpzaamheid.

• Betaling volgens CAO Particuliere Beveiliging Schaal 5;
• Doorgroeimogelijkheden. Securitas is een groot bedrijf. Wij helpen jou verder groeien!;
• Onregelmatigheidstoeslag afhankelijk van jouw type dienst;
• Reiskostenvergoeding, pensioenregeling en eindejaarsuitkering;
• Ontwikkelingsmogelijkheden via onze eigen Learning Hub;
• Benefits at Work app; boordevol kortingen op allerlei winkels en dagjes uit.

We are Kaizen Gaming

Kaizen Gaming, the team powering Betano, is one of the biggest GameTech companies in the world, operating in 20 markets. We always aim to leverage cutting-edge technology, providing the best experience to our millions of customers who trust us for their entertainment.

We are a diverse team of more than 2.700 Kaizeners, from 40+ nationalities spreading across 3 continents.

Our #oneteam is proud to be among the Best Workplaces in Europe and certified Great Place to Work across our offices. Here, there’ll be no average day for you. Ready to Press Play on Potential?

Let’s start with the role

The Content Specialist will plan and execute the brand’s content strategy throughout its various online and offline touchpoints, acting as a liaison with publishers, agencies and third parties and supporting all relevant communications of the local and international marketing teams.

This role is focused on a range of content-driven activities, with specific emphasis on optimizing the customer’s journey and its alignment across our communication channels, as well as ensuring the successful localization and contributing to the successful fulfillment of all content-related requirements throughout the organization.

As a Content Specialist, you will:

• Plan and deliver the editorial calendar on a monthly basis to ensure on-time content delivery;

• Utilize all applicable content formats to share a unique content experience with members and partners;

• Provide writing, editing and proofreading support for ad hoc copy requests, for example new offers or products, campaigns, newsletters and projects;

• Contact external partners (journalists, bloggers, influencers etc.) with content distribution requests;

• Establish and develop good relationships with external partners;

• Monitor and report on published content;

• Monitor and maintain content on the main platform on site and suggest updates where needed;

• Work with local and International Marketing and Product teams;

• Ensure content’s alignment with the brand’s tone of voice and style guide, produce and/or provide guidelines to publishers for native content creation;

• Data/ info mining for rich/interactive content creation (stats/infographics, videos, trivia);

• Monitor competition;

• Act proactively on new ideas on content formats and distribution;

• Support ad hoc social media content needs and campaign rollouts as required;

• Ad hoc social media responsibilities as needed.

What you will bring:

• Degree in Marketing / Communications / Media or other relevant fields;

• Native-level proficiency in Finnish, excellent command of Swedish, and good command of English.

• Min. 2 years of relevant experience;

• Ideally, have a background in sports betting content creation and/or experience in sports/online sports editorial;

• Strong understanding of digital/online technology and its application;

• Experience in content management systems (CMS) and SEO practices;

• Adeptness in working in a fast-paced environment;

• Self-motivation, flexibility and being a team-player.

• Social media experience is a plus

Kaizen Gaming Perks

• 🕑 Hybrid way of working 🏃 A buddy will support you with your onboarding 💸 Competitive pay and bonus scheme 👩‍⚕️ Private health insurance for you and your family ⭐Developmental 360° feedback framework 📚 Unlimited access to Udemy & continuous training 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 Family Support

